course: dictionary
lesson: 453
title: Arid and dry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Arid means very dry. An arid place gets so little rain that few plants can grow there. «Australia is the driest inhabited continent, and about 70 percent of it is arid or semi-arid land, so most Australians live near the coast.» The clues are driest and near the coast: land that is very dry is hard to live on, so people gather by the sea.
explain: Check the clues in the sentence. Arid is linked with driest, so it must mean dry. Try the swap: "about 70 percent of it is dry or semi-dry land" still makes sense, so your meaning is right. Semi- means partly, so semi-arid means partly dry.
explain: Arid can also describe something dull, with no life or interest in it. The clues tell you which meaning fits: arid land is about rain and plants, but an arid talk is about how boring it is.
fact: Arid means very dry, with very little rain.
fact: «Arid» land has so little water that few plants can grow there.
fact: «Semi-arid» means partly dry: it gets some rain, but less than most places.
fact: Plants and animals in deserts have special ways to save water. Cacti store water, and camels can go a long time without drinking.
fact: Figurative use: an arid lesson or talk is dull and boring, with no life or interest in it.
exercise: «Australia is the driest inhabited continent, and about 70 percent of it is arid or semi-arid land.» What does arid mean? | Full of tall trees | Very cold, with lots of snow | *Very dry, with very little rain | Very wet and muddy
exercise: Find and copy the word in the sentence that tells you arid means dry. | *driest | coast | continent | inhabited
exercise: Mr Hale says his lesson was so arid. What does he mean? | *Dull and boring, with no life or interest | Full of water and plants | Cold and icy | Very loud and exciting
test: What does «semi-arid» mean? | *Partly dry, not as dry as a desert | Wet all year round | Completely dry, with no rain at all | Covered in ice
test: Why are camels and cacti able to survive in arid places? | They fly away from the heat | They only live in cold places | *They have special ways to save water | They never need any water
exam: Which word could replace arid in «The arid land had no rivers»? | Noisy | Wet | *Dry | Green
